{
  "task_id": 369,
  "ref_idx": 0,
  "model": "claude-sonnet-5",
  "code": "import backtrader as bt\n\n\nclass MeanReversionBandStrategy(bt.Strategy):\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.ema20 = bt.indicators.EMA(self.data.close, period=20)\n        self.ema_mean = bt.indicators.SMA(self.ema20, period=20)\n        self.ema_std = bt.indicators.StdDev(self.ema20, period=20)\n        self.upper_band = self.ema_mean + 2.0 * self.ema_std\n        self.lower_band = self.ema_mean - 2.0 * self.ema_std\n\n        self.cross_lower = bt.indicators.CrossOver(self.ema20, self.lower_band)\n        self.cross_upper = bt.indicators.CrossOver(self.ema20, self.upper_band)\n        self.cross_mean = bt.indicators.CrossOver(self.ema20, self.ema_mean)\n\n        self.order = None\n        self.stop_order = None\n\n    def notify_order(self, order):\n        if order.status in [order.Submitted, order.Accepted]:\n            return\n\n        if order.status == order.Completed:\n            if order.exectype == bt.Order.Stop:\n                self.stop_order = None\n                self.order = None\n            elif not self.position:\n                self.order = None\n            else:\n                entry_price = order.executed.price\n                if order.isbuy():\n                    stop_price = entry_price * 0.98\n                    self.order = None\n                    self.stop_order = self.sell(exectype=bt.Order.Stop, price=stop_price)\n                else:\n                    stop_price = entry_price * 1.02\n                    self.order = None\n                    self.stop_order = self.buy(exectype=bt.Order.Stop, price=stop_price)\n\n        elif order.status in [order.Canceled, order.Margin, order.Rejected]:\n            if order.exectype == bt.Order.Stop:\n                self.stop_order = None\n            else:\n                self.order = None\n\n    def next(self):\n        if self.order:\n            return\n\n        if not self.position:\n            if self.cross_lower[0] > 0:\n                self.order = self.buy()\n            elif self.cross_upper[0] < 0:\n                self.order = self.sell()\n        else:\n            if self.cross_mean[0] != 0:\n                if self.stop_order:\n                    self.cancel(self.stop_order)\n                self.order = self.close()",
  "assumptions": [
    {
      "topic": "stop-loss implementation",
      "choice": "Entries are submitted as market orders (self.buy()/self.sell()); on fill, a separate stop order (exectype=bt.Order.Stop) is submitted at entry_price*0.98 (long) or entry_price*1.02 (short) to realize the stated 2% protective stop.",
      "reason": "Spec states entry is 'at market' and a stop-loss is 'attached' at 2% from the (actual) entry fill price; backtrader has no single-call construct for a market entry plus attached stop other than issuing the stop as a follow-up order once the fill price is known."
    },
    {
      "topic": "exit-signal direction",
      "choice": "The exit ('EMA20 crosses EMA_mean') is treated as any crossing (upward or downward) of EMA20 through EMA_mean, applied identically regardless of whether the open position is long or short.",
      "reason": "The spec states the exit condition once, without conditioning direction on position side, so it is implemented literally as a bidirectional cross."
    },
    {
      "topic": "stop/exit order conflict",
      "choice": "If the EMA20/EMA_mean exit signal fires while a protective stop order is still live, the stop order is canceled before the close() order is submitted.",
      "reason": "Spec does not address the case of both exit mechanisms being simultaneously eligible; canceling the now-redundant stop avoids two competing orders on one position, which the environment's single-position constraint requires."
    }
  ],
